<title>USA: Wal-Mart sets buy back, dividend increase.</title>
<headline>Wal-Mart sets buy back, dividend increase.</headline>
<dateline>BENTONVILLE, Ark. 1997-03-06</dateline>
<text>
<p>Wal-Mart Stores Inc said Thursday it plans to buy back $2 billion worth of its stock over the next 12 to 18 months, and has increased its dividend by 29 percent.</p>
<p>The company said it expects to announce additions to the share repurchase program.  The shares to be repurchased are expected to represent less than four percent of the company's currently outstanding shares.</p>
<p>Wal-Mart said it raised its annual cash dividend rate to $0.27 per share, which will be payable quarterly at $0.0675. The prior quarterly rate was $0.0525 per share.</p>
<p>The first quarterly dividend at the new rate is payable April 9 to shareholders of record on March 19.</p>
